==============================================================================
§6 PG-SC-09 — the world where attaching usage is WRONG, and why the slice still ships
==============================================================================
World: the provider does NOT bill a parse-failed 200 (no-choices / zero-usage), so recording
the body's usage would OVERSTATE spend and over-count toward the monthly cap. Disposition:
the row records what the body CARRIED (the raw usage dict, unmodified) and the cost is computed
by the file's OWN existing `compute_cost` line — the same arithmetic the success path uses, so
the split is not invented. The reader and both service writers preserve the SG-030 contract
("what the exception carries"), the `error_state` column labels the row as a failure, and the
zero/absent case stays honestly `0.0`/absent. A later slice can decide billing semantics from
the labelled rows; this slice only stops discarding data the wire delivered.
